===Climate===
Aizawa Prefecture has a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification ''Cfa''), characterized by hot, humid summers and mild winters. The western coast, facing the Shendan Ocean, receives heavy rainfall during the typhoon season (November–April), and the [[Asuka Range]] creates a significant rain shadow effect — the coastal plain receives approximately 2,200 mm of precipitation annually, while the mountain interior receives over 3,500 mm. The volcanic activity of the Asuka Range provides geothermal energy and numerous hot springs throughout the prefecture.

